%% W2D4 — Custom MCP Server Build — Request Flow
%% Shows the full MCP session lifecycle: initialize, tool discovery, tool call, and error handling
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Agent as AI Agent Runtime
    participant Client as MCP Client
    participant Server as MCP Server
    participant Handler as Tool Handler
    participant Backend as Backend Service

    User->>Agent: Submit task requiring tool use
    Agent->>Client: Start MCP session
    Client->>Server: initialize (protocolVersion, clientInfo)
    Server-->>Client: serverInfo, capabilities
    Client->>Server: initialized (notification)

    Note over Client,Server: Session established — tool discovery begins

    Client->>Server: tools/list
    Server-->>Client: Tool definitions with JSON Schemas
    Client-->>Agent: Available tools + schemas

    Agent->>Agent: LLM selects tool and generates arguments
    Agent->>Client: Invoke tool with arguments

    Client->>Server: tools/call (tool_name, arguments)
    Server->>Server: Validate arguments against JSON Schema

    alt Validation passes
        Server->>Handler: Dispatch with validated arguments
        Handler->>Backend: Execute scoped operation
        Backend-->>Handler: Raw result
        Handler-->>Server: Structured result
        Server-->>Client: content array (TextContent)
        Client-->>Agent: Tool result
        Agent-->>User: Final response incorporating result
    else Validation fails — missing required field
        Server-->>Client: JSON-RPC error -32602 (Invalid params)
        Client-->>Agent: Structured error with field name
        Agent->>Agent: Error handling loop — retry or escalate
        Agent-->>User: Diagnostic message
    end
